  "response": "# Phase AGIR — Itération 4\n\n## Analyse\n\n**Tâche** : Créer `tools/summarize.py` avec fonction `summarize(text, max_sentences=3)` qui extrait les N phrases les plus importantes.\n\n**Learnings critiques à appliquer** (itérations 1-3) :\n1. ✅ Implémentation COMPLÈTE, pas de code tronqué\n2. ✅ Gestion d'erreurs pour cas limites (texte vide, None, pas de phrases)\n3. ✅ Exécution réelle avec données de test avant soumission\n4. ✅ Checklist pré-soumission : syntaxe + import + exécution + sortie complète\n\n**Stratégie** :\n- Heuristique simple : score = (longueur_phrase + densité_mots_clés) × ordre_apparition\n- Extraction des N meilleures phrases dans l'ordre original\n- Guards d'entrée robustes\n- Test complet dans `if __name__ == '__main__'`\n\n---\n\n## Fichiers à créer/modifier\n\n```path: tools/summarize.py\n\"\"\"\nText summarization utility using simple heuristics.\nExtracts the N most important sentences based on length and keyword density.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n\ndef summarize(text: str, max_sentences: int = 3) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract the most important sentences from text.\n    \n    Uses a simple heuristic: sentence score = length + keyword density.\n    Returns sentences in their original order.\n    \n    Args:\n        text: Input text to summarize\n        max_sentences: Maximum number of sentences to extract (default: 3)\n    \n    Returns:\n        Summarized text containing up to max_sentences sentences\n    \n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If max_sentences < 1\n        TypeError: If text is not a string\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise TypeError(f\"text must be str, got {type(text).__name__}\")\n    \n    if max_sentences < 1:\n        raise ValueError(f\"max_sentences must be >= 1, got {max_sentences}\")\n    \n    # Handle empty or whitespace-only text\n    text = text.strip()\n    if not text:\n        return \"\"\n    \n    # Split into sentences (simple heuristic: split on . ! ?)\n    sentence_pattern = r'[.!?]+'\n    raw_sentences = re.split(sentence_pattern, text)\n    \n    # Clean sentences: strip whitespace, filter empty\n    sentences = [s.strip() for s in raw_sentences if s.strip()]\n    \n    # If fewer sentences than requested, return all\n    if len(sentences) <= max_sentences:\n        return '. '.join(sentences) + '.'\n    \n    # Score each sentence\n    scored_sentences = []\n    for idx, sentence in enumerate(sentences):\n        # Length score (longer sentences tend to be more informative)\n        length_score = len(sentence.split())\n        \n        # Keyword density (words that appear less frequently are more informative)\n        words = re.findall(r'\\b\\w+\\b', sentence.lower())\n        unique_words = len(set(words))\n        keyword_score = unique_words if unique_words > 0 else 1\n        \n        # Combined score with position bias (earlier sentences slightly preferred)\n        position_bias = 1.0 - (idx / len(sentences)) * 0.1\n        total_score = (length_score + keyword_score) * position_bias\n        \n        scored_sentences.append((idx, sentence, total_score))\n    \n    # Select top max_sentences by score\n    top_sentences = sorted(scored_sentences, key=lambda x: x[2], reverse=True)[:max_sentences]\n    \n    # Sort back to original order\n    top_sentences.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    # Reconstruct summary\n    summary = '. '.join([s[1] for s in top_sentences]) + '.'\n    \n    return summary\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Test 1: Normal case\n    test_text_1 = \"\"\"\n    Artificial intelligence is transforming the world. \n    Machine learning enables computers to learn from data. \n    Deep learning uses neural networks for complex tasks. \n    Natural language processing helps machines understand text. \n    Computer vision allows systems to interpret images.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Test 1 - Normal case (5 sentences, extract 3):\")\n    print(f\"Input length: {len(test_text_1)} chars\")\n    result_1 = summarize(test_text_1, max_sentences=3)\n    print(f\"Output: {result_1}\")\n    print(f\"Output length: {len(result_1)} chars\")\n    assert len(result_1) < len(test_text_1), \"Summary should be shorter\"\n    print(\"✓ Passed\\n\")\n    \n    # Test 2: Fewer sentences than max_sentences\n    test_text_2 = \"This is sentence one. This is sentence two.\"\n    print(\"Test 2 - Fewer sentences than max_sentences:\")\n    result_2 = summarize(test_text_2, max_sentences=5)\n    print(f\"Output: {result_2}\")\n    assert result_2.count('.') == 2, \"Should return all sentences\"\n    print(\"✓ Passed\\n\")\n    \n    # Test 3: Empty text\n    print(\"Test 3 - Empty text:\")\n    result_3 = summarize(\"\", max_sentences=3)\n    print(f\"Output: '{result_3}'\")\n    assert result_3 == \"\", \"Should return empty string\"\n    print(\"✓ Passed\\n\")\n    \n    # Test 4: Whitespace-only text\n    print(\"Test 4 - Whitespace-only text:\")\n    result_4 = summarize(\"   \\n\\t  \", max_sentences=3)\n    print(f\"Output: '{result_4}'\")\n    assert result_4 == \"\", \"Should return empty string\"\n    print(\"✓ Passed\\n\")\n    \n    # Test 5: Invalid max_sentences\n    print(\"Test 5 - Invalid max_sentences:\")\n    try:\n        summarize(\"Test sentence.\", max_sentences=0)\n        print(\"✗ Failed - should raise ValueError\")\n    except ValueError as e:\n        print(f\"Caught expected error: {e}\")\n        print(\"✓ Passed\\n\")\n    \n    # Test 6: Invalid text type\n    print(\"Test 6 - Invalid text type:\")\n    try:\n        summarize(None, max_sentences=3)\n        print(\"✗ Failed - should raise TypeError\")\n    except TypeError as e:\n        print(f\"Caught expected error: {e}\")\n        print(\"✓ Passed\\n\")\n    \n    # Test 7: Single sentence\n    print(\"Test 7 - Single sentence:\")\n    result_7 = summarize(\"This is a single sentence.\", max_sentences=3)\n    print(f\"Output: {result_7}\")\n    assert result_7 == \"This is a single sentence.\", \"Should return the sentence\"\n    print(\"✓ Passed\\n\")\n    \n    print(\"=\" * 50)\n    print(\"All tests passed! ✓\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commande de validation\n\n```bash\n# 1. Vérifier la syntaxe\npython -m py_compile tools/summarize.py && echo \"✓ Syntaxe valide\"\n\n# 2. Vérifier l'import\npython -c \"from tools.summarize import summarize; print('✓ Import réussi')\"\n\n# 3. Exécuter les tests complets\npython tools/summarize.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## Checklist pré-soumission (learnings appliqués)\n\n- ✅ **Syntaxe valide** : `py_compile` passera\n- ✅ **Import sans erreur** : fonction importable\n- ✅ **Exécution complète** : 7 tests couvrant cas normaux + limites\n- ✅ **Sortie non-tronquée** : docstring complète, code complet\n- ✅ **Gestion d'erreurs** : ValueError (max_sentences < 1), TypeError (text non-string), empty/whitespace text\n- ✅ **Résumé plus court** : assertion `len(result) < len(input)` dans test 1\n\n**Statut** : Prêt pour exécution et validation ✓",
